Subject: seccomp allow guest-driven VFIO interrupt programming on vCPU threads
Why: AC-T7.4.1: change 0001 enables, switches and disables a passthrough device's MSI/MSI-X when the guest programs the capability or MSI-X table (VfioSources::synchronize from write_config_register and MSI-X table writes), on vCPU threads, through ioctl VFIO_DEVICE_SET_IRQS (_IO(';', 100 + 10) = 0x3b6e = 15214, linux/vfio.h). Upstream at this pin calls it once at device setup, before start_vcpus applies the filters, so its vCPU filter allows KVM_IRQFD and KVM_SET_GSI_ROUTING but not this request, and a release VMM dies of SIGSYS at the guest's first MSI/MSI-X enable. Reproduced: the pinned x86_64 vcpu program compiled by this tree's seccompiler-bin traps 0x3b6e (exit 159) while 0x4020ae76 and 0x4008ae6a pass. Only the vcpu filter gains the request; teardown on the vmm thread still resets the device without it.

